    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lrml6jr",
      "content": "Genetics is the branch of biology that studies heredity and variation in living organisms. It explains how traits are transmitted from parents to offspring through genes. In nursing examinations such as RRB Nursing, important topics include DNA structure, chromosomes, Mendelian inheritance, genetic disorders, mutations, and basic genetic terminology."
    },
    {
      "id": "f9nvmdj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Basic Genetic Terminology"
    },
    {
      "id": "7bx0xdz",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Term</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gene</p>",
            "<p>Basic unit of heredity located on chromosomes</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Allele</p>",
            "<p>Alternative form of a gene</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Genotype</p>",
            "<p>Genetic makeup of an individual</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Phenotype</p>",
            "<p>Observable characteristics of an individual</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Homozygous</p>",
            "<p>Two identical alleles for a trait</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Heterozygous</p>",
            "<p>Two different alleles for a trait</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dominant gene</p>",
            "<p>Gene that expresses its effect even if only one copy is present</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Recessive gene</p>",
            "<p>Gene expressed only when two copies are present</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1ouy0y6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Chromosomes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tddn6l2",
      "content": "Chromosomes are thread-like structures located in the nucleus of cells. They are made of DNA and proteins and carry genetic information."
    },
    {
      "id": "pptez52",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Chromosome Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Autosomes</p>",
            "<p>22 pairs of chromosomes controlling body traits</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sex chromosomes</p>",
            "<p>1 pair determining sex (XX in females, XY in males)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
