    {
      "id": "0zbjho9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mendel's Laws of Inheritance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "swg8dxi",
      "content": "Gregor Mendel is known as the father of genetics. His experiments on pea plants led to the formulation of basic laws of inheritance."
    },
    {
      "id": "zdx0k4f",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Law</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Dominance</p>",
            "<p>Dominant allele masks the effect of recessive allele</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Segregation</p>",
            "<p>Alleles separate during gamete formation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Independent Assortment</p>",
            "<p>Genes of different traits assort independently</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
